  "problem_text": "A national consumer brand plans a multi-region campaign across 6 regional markets. The brand can purchase 50 pre-negotiated media bundles. If a bundle is purchased, it delivers a fixed number of standardized exposure units in every region (the delivered units per bundle and region are given in the data). Exposures add up linearly across selected bundles, and each bundle can be purchased at most once. Each region has a target of exposures to reach during the campaign (targets range from 1116 to 1353, total 7286). Because of contractual limits and over-saturation concerns, the brand is not allowed to exceed any regional target. If a region falls short of its target, the shortfall is recorded as an unmet-demand variable and incurs a penalty of 1 per unit. Bundles have no direct purchase cost in this instance, so the decision is to select which bundles to buy to minimize total unmet exposure across all regions.",
